{
  "title": "iOS UI job timeouts discard test failure artifacts and build caches",
  "description": "In iOS run 34253129754 (PR #687), the UI job spent roughly 18 minutes installing/building the backend and CLI. testRecipeFlow then failed before the 30-minute job timeout, but xcodebuild had not exited when cancellation occurred. \
The failure-only artifact upload and both cache post-steps were skipped, losing the login screenshots and xcresult bundle and preventing the expensive cold build from warming the next run. \
Improve the workflow so completed build caches and test diagnostics survive job cancellation; investigate build duplication or split build/test stages instead of just increasing the timeout. \
The original logs remain available on GitHub. \
This issue concerns CI artifact/cache handling; the login failure is being investigated in #687.",
